/-!
# Small certificates for the Parrott Sylow-two normal forms

For each pair `i < j`, conjugating `si` by `sj` is an explicit word in the
preceding generators. These 28 equations are checked pointwise by the kernel.
The 2048 ordered products are distinguished by their images of points 0 and
930: a packed lookup table is a candidate left inverse, whose correctness is
also checked by the kernel. No multiplication table is needed.

The underlying permutations and conventions are those of Parrott (1972),
p. 683; see `refs/original/n-group-global/parrott-tits-presentation.md`.
-/

namespace Tits.Atlas1600SylowTwoCertificate

